  "genie_instructions": "DOMAIN CONTEXT\nThis space supports product and process traceability for a chemicals manufacturer subject to REACH, GHS, TSCA, and responsible-care audits. Regulators and customers increasingly demand sub-4-hour lot trace for recall response and provenance attestations. Stakeholders: Quality Director (genealogy completeness, recall hours, audit findings), Supply Chain VP (supplier audit cadence, quarantined / recalled inventory), CFO (held-lot working capital and recall write-down risk).\n\nMETRIC DEFINITIONS\n- Traceability score = AVG(traceability_score_pct); target ≥ 95% genealogy completeness\n- Recall readiness = AVG(recall_readiness_hours); regulatory target < 4 hours end-to-end\n- Quality pass rate = passed_quality_checks / total_production_events; target ≥ 95%\n- Failed quality checks = events with quality_check_result = 'Fail'; root-cause investigation trigger\n- Process step yield = output_quantity_kg / NULLIF(input_quantity_kg, 0); material efficiency by step\n- Lots with full genealogy / lots produced = audit-readiness ratio\n- Quality holds = lots placed on quality hold; held-inventory exposure\n- Supplier audits completed = compliance cadence; target ≥ 1 per critical supplier per year\n\nQUERY GUIDANCE\n- ALWAYS prefer metric views with MEASURE() syntax for aggregations.\n  - production_events_metrics (source: production_events) — dims: event_date, product_category, facility_id, process_step, supplier_id, quality_check_result; measures: total_production_events, total_input_kg, total_output_kg, passed_quality_checks, failed_quality_checks, unique_lot_count, unique_product_count, max_input_quantity_kg.\n  - traceability_monthly_metrics (source: traceability_monthly) — dims: report_month, product_category, product_id; measures: total_lots_produced, total_lots_full_genealogy, avg_traceability_score, avg_recall_readiness_hours, total_quality_holds, max_lots_produced, total_supplier_audits_completed.\n- Use GROUP BY ALL with MEASURE() queries.\n- For monthly trends, always wrap the date in DATE_TRUNC('month', <date_col>).\n- For \"Top X\" requests, return LIMIT 10 unless the user specifies otherwise.\n- Query base tables directly only when needing columns not exposed by metric views (e.g. product_name, lot_number, lot_status, quantity_on_hand_kg, shelf_life_remaining_days, storage_temp_c).\n- When the user's phrasing matches a SQL snippet display name (filters, expressions, or measures), prefer that snippet.",
  "sample_questions": [
    "Showcase the different visualization options with interesting aspects of the dataset",
